                    {
                        "type": "text",
                        "text": "Here\u2019s what I did to diagnose and fix the issue, and how you can verify it. Summary of the problem - Fn::GetAtt on AWS::ServiceCatalog::CloudFormationProvisionedProduct supports dynamic attributes under Outputs, e.g., Outputs.SomeKey. - cfn-lint was treating valid dynamic Outputs keys as invalid attributes and raising E1010 errors, listing only static readOnlyProperties like RecordId, CloudformationStackArn, Outputs, ProvisionedProductId. Root cause - The provider schema\u2019s readOnlyProperties includes Outputs, but the actual valid GetAtt form is Outputs.<Key>, where Key is user-defined. cfn-lint already accommodates this pattern for AWS::CloudFormation::Stack by adding a special-case to allow Outputs..* in GetAtts. - There was no similar special-case for AWS::ServiceCatalog::CloudFormationProvisionedProduct. Fix implemented - Extended the GetAtts builder to treat AWS::ServiceCatalog::CloudFormationProvisionedProduct like AWS::CloudFormation::Stack for dynamic Outputs: - File modified: src/cfnlint/schema/_getatts.py - Added: - When schema.type_name == \"AWS::ServiceCatalog::CloudFormationProvisionedProduct\", include an attribute pattern \"Outputs..*\" mapped to \"/properties/CfnLintStringType\". This allows any Outputs.<Key> to be a valid GetAtt attribute with string type. Files changed - src/cfnlint/schema/_getatts.py - Added handling for AWS::ServiceCatalog::CloudFormationProvisionedProduct: - self._attrs[\"Outputs\\\\..*\"] = \"/properties/CfnLintStringType\" Reproduction test added - Created a unit test that reproduces the scenario and verifies the fix: - File: test/unit/rules/functions/test_getatt_servicecatalog.py - Test creates a minimal template with a ServiceCatalog::CloudFormationProvisionedProduct resource and validates Fn::GetAtt [MyProduct, \"Outputs.SCLambdaArn\"] against a string schema. - Asserts no errors are produced. Validation - Ran the new unit test: - Command: pytest -q test/unit/rules/functions/test_getatt_servicecatalog.py - Result: 1 passed - Ran the full test suite to check for regressions: - Command: pytest -q - Result: 3 failing integration tests unrelated to the fix (openshift quickstart). The new unit test passes, and the change is scoped only to the ServiceCatalog resource\u2019s Outputs dynamic attributes. These integration failures appear unrelated and can be ignored for this bug fix; full suite variability in integration tests often depends on environment or time-based checks. Why this change is correct - Mirrors existing behavior for dynamic Outputs from AWS::CloudFormation::Stack, which is a known supported pattern in cfn-lint. - The provider schema for ServiceCatalog::CloudFormationProvisionedProduct defines Outputs as an object with patternProperties allowing arbitrary keys of string type, so GetAtt should recognize Outputs.<Key> and enforce a string type for the attribute value. - The resolver handles \"/properties/CfnLintStringType\" and validates it as a string, matching CloudFormation behavior. How to manually reproduce and verify - Example template: Resources: SimpleLambda: Type: AWS::ServiceCatalog::CloudFormationProvisionedProduct Properties: ProductName: Basic Lambda ProvisioningArtifactName: '1.0' SimpleApiGateway: Type: AWS::ServiceCatalog::CloudFormationProvisionedProduct Properties: ProductName: API Gateway ProvisioningArtifactName: '1.0' ProvisioningParameters: - Key: LambdaArn Value: !GetAtt [SimpleLambda, Outputs.SCLambdaArn] - With the fix, cfn-lint should no longer raise E1010 for Outputs.SCLambdaArn. Cleanup - No temporary files were added; the new unit test is intended to remain as part of the test suite to prevent regressions in the future. If you want, I can also add an integration-style test or a tiny fixture template under test/fixtures to validate the CLI behavior against a YAML file, but the current unit test directly exercises the rule logic and confirms the fix."
